    "title": "How 'The Masked Singer' Finale Will Be Impacted By Trump's Speech: Will We Miss the Winner Reveal? - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Just Jared ,\n11 hours ago The Masked Singer season 14 is set to wrap up this evening on Fox, but tonight’s episode will feature a major schedule change.\nUnfortunately, the episode will have a long break baked in as the President, Donald Trump , will be making a televised speech at 9pm ET that will air across all of the primetime slots.\nThis means that, at that time, the Fox reality TV competition series will pause. It’s said that the speech will last around 20 minutes.\nKeep reading to find out more…\nDeadline reports that The Masked Singer will take a 20 minute break and then return right where it left off, so you won’t miss any of the action or the winner getting crowned.\nOther TV shows across all the networks will also be impacted, including Survivor on CBS, and Chicago Fire on NBC. The Late Show and The Tonight Show will both also be moved back in order to accommodate the speech.\nStay tuned to Just Jared , as we’ll reveal the winner of The Masked Singer when its revealed later tonight!",
